<title>GREECE: SMEHA PRESIDENT TO MEET EVERT TUES MORNING.</title>
<headline>SMEHA PRESIDENT TO MEET EVERT TUES MORNING.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Athens stock exchange members association president Panagiotis Kondalexis will meet conservative opposition leader Miltiadis Evert on Tuesday morning, sources at SMEHA told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The capital markets commission, the clearing house and the bourse should reveal all those responsible for fraudulent trade activities,&quot; the conservative New Democracy party said in a statement.</p>
<p>As a second general assembly of SMEHA members was about to start it was yet unknown whether the bourse would be open on Tuesday, sources said.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
